WEBVTT

00:00:11.590 --> 00:00:12.580
Kamui...

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:16.640
Brother Aichi didn't show up today either?

00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:20.530
No. We haven't seen him since 
the regional tournament.

00:00:21.110 --> 00:00:25.000
Then he's still upset about Kai...

00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:29.520
I haven't seen Kai since then, either.

00:02:14.850 --> 00:02:15.980
Aichi...

00:02:17.710 --> 00:02:19.500
I can't fight you.

00:02:26.770 --> 00:02:29.420
Why, Kai...?

00:02:38.490 --> 00:02:39.670
This is...

00:02:40.220 --> 00:02:45.260
The Black Vanguard

00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:56.350
Hey, it's that kid!

00:02:56.600 --> 00:02:58.370
He's here earlier than expected, huh?

00:02:58.760 --> 00:03:00.170
Are you happy, Kourin?

00:03:00.590 --> 00:03:01.290
Idiot!

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:04.410
What do you think? Do we tell him now?

00:03:04.670 --> 00:03:08.070
That he's one of the ones that 
we've been looking for...

00:03:09.590 --> 00:03:10.870
Let's play it by ear.

00:03:14.870 --> 00:03:16.280
I wonder why...

00:03:16.280 --> 00:03:21.310
It feels like something incredibly 
important is going to happen here...

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:23.260
Welcome.

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:26.920
Are you looking for a 
card today or something?

00:03:28.010 --> 00:03:28.920
N-No...

00:03:29.960 --> 00:03:32.410
I don't really know...

00:03:34.320 --> 00:03:36.500
What's wrong? You look a little down.

00:03:36.710 --> 00:03:39.050
You realize you'll be able to play 
in the national tournament...

00:03:39.510 --> 00:03:41.390
Come on! Smile, smile!

00:03:41.870 --> 00:03:43.940
Um... please tell me!

00:03:44.430 --> 00:03:46.660
Was I really strong?

00:03:47.010 --> 00:03:49.090
Yes. You were great.

00:03:49.470 --> 00:03:51.760
It was thrilling to watch,

00:03:51.760 --> 00:03:53.430
the way you clobbered 
your opponent like crazy!

00:03:54.050 --> 00:03:55.200
I see...

00:03:55.590 --> 00:03:57.900
So I was strong...

00:03:58.290 --> 00:03:59.290
And yet...

00:03:59.890 --> 00:04:01.020
Why...?

00:04:01.540 --> 00:04:03.650
Why did Kai say....?

00:04:05.260 --> 00:04:07.470
You should become <i>stronger.</i>

00:04:09.620 --> 00:04:11.140
Ren Suzugamori!

00:04:12.740 --> 00:04:16.610
Do that, and Kai will 
appear before you again.

00:04:17.360 --> 00:04:21.380
The stronger the player, the 
more value he finds in them.

00:04:21.550 --> 00:04:23.350
That's the kind of guy Kai is.

00:04:24.390 --> 00:04:26.100
I'm getting that sensation again.

00:04:27.140 --> 00:04:28.990
Could I have come here...

00:04:29.170 --> 00:04:31.210
to meet him?!

00:04:34.490 --> 00:04:36.140
What is he doing here?!

00:04:36.490 --> 00:04:40.440
The two that we were 
looking for are both here!

00:04:40.440 --> 00:04:41.540
What do <i>you</i> want?!

00:04:42.020 --> 00:04:44.560
That's quite a cold reception.

00:04:44.970 --> 00:04:49.280
Even though we're important 
"customers" to you...

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:52.930
I came here today...

00:04:53.290 --> 00:04:56.290
because I had a hunch that 
something nice would happen.

00:04:57.230 --> 00:04:59.800
Long time no see, Aichi Sendou.

00:05:01.620 --> 00:05:06.020
While you were fighting, you experienced 
a particular sensation, didn't you?

00:05:06.340 --> 00:05:08.770
Like the cards were calling to you...

00:05:09.590 --> 00:05:11.000
How did you know?

00:05:11.180 --> 00:05:14.790
Your strength grew because 
you have awakened that power.

00:05:15.270 --> 00:05:16.160
Incidentally...

00:05:16.790 --> 00:05:19.120
I have that power, too.

00:05:22.400 --> 00:05:26.290
Only the chosen possess that power.

00:05:26.670 --> 00:05:30.240
The reason I've won every 
match fight up to now...

00:05:30.240 --> 00:05:32.660
is because of that gift.

00:05:32.660 --> 00:05:34.380
It's a wonderful power.

00:05:35.290 --> 00:05:37.060
And, even better...

00:05:37.060 --> 00:05:40.310
you can develop it further.

00:05:40.690 --> 00:05:44.140
That's right. You can grow stronger still.

00:05:45.630 --> 00:05:48.330
Why are you telling me this?

00:05:49.020 --> 00:05:51.680
I'm going to give you a excellent present.

00:05:52.430 --> 00:05:56.900
If you use this, you'll 
expand your power even more.

00:06:00.110 --> 00:06:01.970
A Shadow Paladin deck!

00:06:15.830 --> 00:06:17.810
You felt it just now, didn't you?

00:06:18.190 --> 00:06:20.710
This deck's phenomenal strength...

00:06:21.010 --> 00:06:22.890
What is that deck?

00:06:22.890 --> 00:06:24.660
It's a Shadow Paladin deck.

00:06:25.860 --> 00:06:29.790
You gain overwhelming strength 
by sacrificing your allies.

00:06:30.130 --> 00:06:33.530
It's the exact opposite of 
your Royal Paladin deck.

00:06:35.910 --> 00:06:39.950
I do think everyone has a 
deck that befits them...

00:06:50.020 --> 00:06:54.550
Aichi, you wanna get stronger, 
don't you? For Kai's sake...

00:06:56.710 --> 00:06:58.450
Picture it!

00:07:05.620 --> 00:07:07.710
You hesitate because you're weak.

00:07:09.110 --> 00:07:11.080
You don't like to be weak, do you?

00:07:13.120 --> 00:07:16.260
Now, take this deck.

00:07:17.100 --> 00:07:20.920
Take it, and it will give you strength.

00:07:23.760 --> 00:07:28.450
In order to meet Kai again, 
you must get stronger.

00:08:01.060 --> 00:08:04.190
I-Incredible! How powerful is this deck?!

00:08:04.510 --> 00:08:07.000
Despair to the powerless...

00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:11.480
And all the glory to the one with the power!

00:08:22.230 --> 00:08:25.120
Shadow Paladin, the deck in which 
you sacrifice your allies...

00:08:26.670 --> 00:08:28.390
Ludicrous...

00:08:28.730 --> 00:08:32.480
You really think you can get 
stronger just by using that deck?!

00:08:35.760 --> 00:08:36.960
Oh, really?

00:08:37.540 --> 00:08:39.860
Then fight me and you'll understand...

00:08:40.750 --> 00:08:43.360
That deck can't give you any strength!

00:08:45.340 --> 00:08:48.070
Well? Are we gonna do it? Or not?

00:08:51.370 --> 00:08:52.950
I'll keep you company.

00:08:58.910 --> 00:09:01.490
This is my Shadow Paladin's first battle...

00:09:20.180 --> 00:09:21.840
Things are really heating up...

00:09:22.050 --> 00:09:24.350
I wonder how this fight will go...

00:09:24.640 --> 00:09:25.370
Suiko...

00:09:25.670 --> 00:09:28.800
Still, if he really has gotten 
stronger than before...

00:09:29.450 --> 00:09:32.520
That suits our purpose, too.

00:09:39.060 --> 00:09:41.110
Stand up, Vanguard!

00:09:42.510 --> 00:09:43.500
Brugal!

00:09:43.500 --> 00:09:44.210
Fullbau!

00:09:46.280 --> 00:09:48.070
So, you're playing with a Royal Paladin deck.

00:09:48.410 --> 00:09:51.620
I'll show you the strength of this clan...

00:09:51.950 --> 00:09:53.300
like you've never seen before!

00:10:10.540 --> 00:10:13.900
This is the first time he's 
used a Shadow Paladin deck...

00:10:14.140 --> 00:10:16.150
How well will he be able to use it?

00:10:17.050 --> 00:10:18.730
Both of you, good luck!

00:10:19.130 --> 00:10:21.410
It's my turn and I draw.

00:10:22.690 --> 00:10:25.210
I ride Lake Maiden, Lien!

00:10:29.250 --> 00:10:31.750
Brugal moves to the rear-guard circle.

00:10:32.380 --> 00:10:34.160
I activate Lien's skill.

00:10:34.930 --> 00:10:36.170
I'm changing a card.

00:10:40.090 --> 00:10:41.310
That's the end of my turn.

00:10:42.130 --> 00:10:43.360
My turn.

00:10:45.700 --> 00:10:47.710
I ride Blaster Javelin!

00:10:52.440 --> 00:10:54.330
Fullbau is in the Soul,

00:10:54.570 --> 00:10:57.040
so Javelin's power becomes 8000.

00:10:58.140 --> 00:11:00.560
And then I activate Fullbau's skill.

00:11:01.550 --> 00:11:04.460
If I ride Blaster Javelin,

00:11:04.930 --> 00:11:06.940
I can search the deck for this card.

00:11:09.460 --> 00:11:10.930
Blaster Dark!

00:11:25.510 --> 00:11:27.030
Watch carefully.

00:11:27.870 --> 00:11:31.240
This will make you fully 
appreciate what power is.

00:11:33.170 --> 00:11:35.440
Yeesh, how conceited!

00:11:35.440 --> 00:11:37.450
But maybe it's just a little cool!

00:11:38.040 --> 00:11:40.910
Blaster Javelin attacks Lien!

00:11:43.700 --> 00:11:45.500
Damage trigger check!

00:11:46.450 --> 00:11:47.450
Go ahead.

00:11:48.920 --> 00:11:52.640
I'm going to make you regret 
your smart-alecky words!

00:11:55.610 --> 00:11:57.530
I ride Beast Knight, Garmall!

00:12:02.900 --> 00:12:04.570
I activate Garmall's skill!

00:12:05.220 --> 00:12:07.740
I discard one Royal Paladin 
card from my hand,

00:12:07.900 --> 00:12:09.800
and Superior Call Snogal!

00:12:13.050 --> 00:12:14.770
And then I call Gallatin!

00:12:19.200 --> 00:12:23.780
I attack Blaster Javelin with Beast 
Knight, Garmall, boosted by Snogal!

00:12:26.500 --> 00:12:28.210
Drive trigger check...

00:12:29.070 --> 00:12:31.090
I got a critical trigger.

00:12:31.560 --> 00:12:33.600
I add +5000 to the power of Gallatin.

00:12:35.770 --> 00:12:38.360
I give the extra critical 
to Beast Knight, Garmall.

00:12:43.620 --> 00:12:46.290
Gallatin attacks with a boost from Blugal!

00:12:52.910 --> 00:12:57.240
Well, that was the first attack, 
so I'll let you off with 3 damage.

00:12:57.840 --> 00:12:59.990
You don't have to take it so seriously.

00:13:00.140 --> 00:13:02.270
After all, it's a foregone conclusion 
that you're going to lose...

00:13:14.240 --> 00:13:15.590
I know.

00:13:15.890 --> 00:13:18.460
You'll lead me to victory, right?

00:13:19.660 --> 00:13:21.390
I could see it, too.

00:13:21.950 --> 00:13:24.360
The moment of your victory...

00:13:29.220 --> 00:13:31.440
Go forth and destroy, my avatar!

00:13:32.840 --> 00:13:34.820
Cleave with your sword of darkness!

00:13:37.800 --> 00:13:40.340
I ride Blaster Dark!

00:13:46.340 --> 00:13:51.810
If Blaster Javelin is in the Soul, then 
Blaster Dark receives +1000 power.

00:13:53.430 --> 00:13:55.240
And then, Counterblast.

00:13:57.100 --> 00:13:59.030
Disappear, Gallatin!

00:14:08.960 --> 00:14:11.070
I call Skull Witch, Nemain.

00:14:13.930 --> 00:14:15.420
Counterblast.

00:14:22.980 --> 00:14:23.890
I call...

00:14:30.530 --> 00:14:32.460
Knight of Darkness, Rugos,

00:14:32.460 --> 00:14:34.560
attack Beast Knight, Garmall!

00:14:39.890 --> 00:14:43.370
Blaster Dark attacks with 
a boost from Doranbau!

00:14:44.600 --> 00:14:47.510
And then I activate Doranbau's skill!

00:14:47.510 --> 00:14:50.020
Blaster Dark receives +4000 power!

00:14:51.690 --> 00:14:52.690
Check!

00:14:53.560 --> 00:14:54.530
I got a trigger.

00:14:55.670 --> 00:14:57.770
I add +5000 to the power of Nemain.

00:14:58.340 --> 00:14:59.970
And then I draw a card.

00:15:08.100 --> 00:15:10.450
Skull Witch, Nemain attacks!

00:15:10.830 --> 00:15:13.550
Oh, no, you don't! I guard with Epona!

00:15:18.730 --> 00:15:20.060
That's the end of my turn.

00:15:20.540 --> 00:15:24.560
This is his first time with a Shadow Paladin 
deck, yet he's already got command of it...

00:15:24.880 --> 00:15:27.040
Is this also the power of Psyqualia?

00:15:27.740 --> 00:15:29.750
Well, I'm not going to lose!

00:15:30.180 --> 00:15:31.490
It's my turn!

00:15:33.160 --> 00:15:34.340
Here I go!

00:15:34.340 --> 00:15:36.280
Enter the fray, Knight of Beasts!

00:15:36.710 --> 00:15:39.900
I ride Fang of Light, Garmall!

00:15:42.120 --> 00:15:45.030
By discarding one Fang of 
Light, Garmall from my hand...

00:15:45.030 --> 00:15:46.940
I can call Snogal or Brugal!

00:15:49.250 --> 00:15:50.720
I call Snogal.

00:15:51.510 --> 00:15:52.880
Snogal's skill!

00:15:54.040 --> 00:15:57.130
For any other Snogal on the field, 
each Snogal receives +1000 power.

00:15:57.810 --> 00:15:59.630
Fang of Light, Garmall's skill!

00:16:01.270 --> 00:16:04.350
Snogal and Brugal, lend your 
power to Fang of Light!

00:16:06.400 --> 00:16:09.070
His power has increased all the 
way to 13000 in an instant!

00:16:09.070 --> 00:16:11.480
Raising power through the 
cooperation of allies...

00:16:11.480 --> 00:16:13.650
That's the Royal Paladin way to do it.

00:16:14.340 --> 00:16:17.220
Ah, that made me realize...

00:16:17.660 --> 00:16:20.600
The way to use Royal Paladin allies...

00:16:20.950 --> 00:16:22.400
It's wishy-washy.

00:16:24.120 --> 00:16:26.370
This just confirms it.

00:16:26.370 --> 00:16:30.150
As long as I have this deck, 
my victory is unshakable.

00:16:30.150 --> 00:16:32.630
We'll see if it really works out like that!

00:16:33.120 --> 00:16:35.280
Brugal and Snogal move!

00:16:37.060 --> 00:16:39.430
I call Knight of Conviction, Bors!

00:16:40.890 --> 00:16:43.760
With a boost from Snogal, Brugal attacks!

00:16:45.430 --> 00:16:47.240
I intercept with Nemain!

00:16:51.800 --> 00:16:55.520
I attack with Fang of Light, 
Garmall, boosted by Snogal!

00:17:00.710 --> 00:17:02.620
Drive trigger check.

00:17:02.620 --> 00:17:04.150
Critical trigger!

00:17:04.340 --> 00:17:06.410
I add +5000 to the power of Bors.

00:17:07.080 --> 00:17:09.320
I give the extra critical to Garmall!

00:17:15.640 --> 00:17:18.330
I attack with Knight of Conviction, Bors!

00:17:18.860 --> 00:17:20.300
I guard with Grim Reaper!

00:17:27.030 --> 00:17:28.570
That's the end of my turn.

00:17:28.570 --> 00:17:30.800
You were just thinking, 'Almost 
got him', weren't you?

00:17:31.940 --> 00:17:36.040
In the end, it's just futile resistance.

00:17:36.040 --> 00:17:38.340
I've already told you 
several times, remember?

00:17:38.720 --> 00:17:41.190
The victor has already been decided.

00:17:42.980 --> 00:17:45.260
That's right. This is going to be my...

00:17:46.190 --> 00:17:47.410
Final Turn!

00:17:59.410 --> 00:18:01.210
Cursed dragon,

00:18:01.210 --> 00:18:04.240
come out and muster your 
dark power! I ride...

00:18:05.090 --> 00:18:07.320
Phantom Blaster Dragon!

00:18:20.110 --> 00:18:21.000
I call...

00:18:26.260 --> 00:18:28.460
I'll show you.

00:18:28.940 --> 00:18:32.930
This is how you use Shadow Paladin allies.

00:18:35.610 --> 00:18:38.370
I activate Phantom Blaster Dragon's skill!

00:18:38.860 --> 00:18:40.160
Counterblast!

00:18:40.330 --> 00:18:43.880
Abyss Freezer! Mac Lir! Doranbau!

00:18:44.080 --> 00:18:46.900
Give your lives to the cursed dragon!

00:19:02.260 --> 00:19:06.830
The Counterblast and three sacrifices 
add +10000 to its power.

00:19:06.830 --> 00:19:08.120
And it gets the extra critical, too.

00:19:08.510 --> 00:19:12.540
This is Phantom Blaster Dragon's 
Damned Charging Lance!

00:19:14.930 --> 00:19:16.430
That's the way.

00:19:16.430 --> 00:19:18.260
You're drunk with power.

00:19:18.780 --> 00:19:22.760
Soon, you won't be able to do 
anything without that power.

00:19:23.970 --> 00:19:25.120
I don't like this...

00:19:26.340 --> 00:19:27.330
I call...

00:19:39.390 --> 00:19:41.690
Abyss Healer boosts...

00:19:41.690 --> 00:19:42.990
as I attack with Rugos!

00:19:50.880 --> 00:19:51.710
Charon!

00:19:54.610 --> 00:19:56.970
Go, Blaster Dragon!

00:19:59.720 --> 00:20:02.420
I guard with two Alabaster Owls and Marron!

00:20:08.160 --> 00:20:10.180
That should be enough to defend me...

00:20:14.180 --> 00:20:15.730
Drive check...

00:20:19.410 --> 00:20:21.250
I could hear your voice...

00:20:22.670 --> 00:20:24.220
Grim Reaper!

00:20:27.930 --> 00:20:29.160
Critical trigger!

00:20:30.270 --> 00:20:32.800
I give all the effects to Blaster Dark!

00:20:36.590 --> 00:20:37.790
Oh, no...

00:20:42.690 --> 00:20:44.490
Please picture this...

00:20:45.530 --> 00:20:48.240
You, standing before me...

00:20:48.870 --> 00:20:50.540
realizing that you're powerless!

00:21:02.290 --> 00:21:03.710
This proves it.

00:21:04.120 --> 00:21:08.620
His Psyqualia is even stronger than before...

00:21:12.100 --> 00:21:14.330
Despair to the powerless...

00:21:17.230 --> 00:21:21.320
And all the glory to the one with the power!

00:21:31.950 --> 00:21:36.050
What...? Is this the power of Psyqualia?

00:21:38.410 --> 00:21:41.890
Wow! He beat Kourin with ease!

00:21:42.180 --> 00:21:44.730
Hey, do you think this means his 
power is completely activated?!

00:21:46.620 --> 00:21:48.260
Shadow Paladin...

00:21:48.640 --> 00:21:52.480
I must have been waiting to meet this deck.

00:21:52.770 --> 00:21:55.200
I won't lose to anyone now...

00:21:57.030 --> 00:22:00.830
I'm stronger than anyone now!

00:22:01.350 --> 00:22:05.310
That's right. You've become 
stronger than anyone.

00:22:05.310 --> 00:22:08.140
Even stronger than your friend Kai...

00:23:51.600 --> 00:23:54.230
Is Brother Aichi never gonna come back?!

00:23:54.530 --> 00:23:56.240
It's all up to him.

00:23:56.790 --> 00:24:00.440
True, when I was down, I 
wanted to be left alone...

00:24:00.440 --> 00:24:04.940
But if he needs help, it would 
be better if we're all there.

00:24:04.940 --> 00:24:06.690
So what should we do?!

00:24:06.690 --> 00:24:07.910
I've gotten strong.

00:24:08.100 --> 00:24:10.820
Kai will give me recognition now!

00:24:10.820 --> 00:24:13.760
I'm sure if I fought Kai now, I would win!

00:24:13.760 --> 00:24:15.860
Next time: Unexpected Visitor!

00:24:15.860 --> 00:24:18.560
I'm getting one picture 
after another in my head...
